  "tagline": "Rust graph-vector database on object storage, queried through typed SDKs for AI apps.",
  "description": "HelixDB is a young open-source database in Rust that keeps entities and relationships in one property graph with native vector and BM25 full-text search, aimed at RAG and agent memory. Version 3 moved storage onto S3-compatible object storage (with in-memory and on-disk modes) and archived its earlier HelixQL language in favor of typed query builders in Rust, TypeScript, Python and Go, or JSON sent to an HTTP endpoint. Helix Cloud offers a managed tier from a few dollars a month. It is promising for AI-centric apps that want graph plus vector in one place, but the API has changed quickly and it lacks a standard query language.",
